From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8350: keep the PCIe GDSCs on across system suspend

System suspend reset the phone on resume: genpd powered pcie_0_gdsc off in
suspend_noirq, and on resume_noirq "pcie_0_gdsc status stuck at 'off'"
(gdsc_toggle_logic), after which the PCIe controller (Wi-Fi, ath11k) was
accessed with its domain down and the SoC took a warm reset.

The PCIe controller cannot resume from a collapsed GDSC. Like gcc-sm8450
and gcc-sm8550, declare the PCIe GDSCs PWRSTS_RET_ON so genpd leaves them
powered through suspend.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c	2026-09-26 16:27:21.934489552 +0200
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8350.c	2026-09-26 16:27:21.947416261 +0200
@@ -3421,7 +3421,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_0_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc pcie_1_gdsc = {
@@ -3429,7 +3429,7 @@
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "pcie_1_gdsc",
 	},
-	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
+	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_RET_ON,
 };
 
 static struct gdsc ufs_card_gdsc = {
